From 0000000000000000000000000000000000000000 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Derek Ross <derekross@gmail.com>
Date: Sun, 11 Oct 2026 19:19:10 -0400
Subject: [PATCH] dt-bindings: gpu: mali-valhall-csf: add Google gs201
 compatible

Google gs201 (Tensor G2) has a Mali-G710 (arch 10.8, product major 2),
a CSF GPU that Panthor drives. Add its SoC-specific compatible, used
with the "arm,mali-valhall-csf" fallback.

On gs201 the GPU rails follow the G3D power domain and the voltage is
set by the APM firmware together with the clock, so the generic
properties are enough and no SoC-specific constraints are added.

Co-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5.5 <noreply@anthropic.com>
---
 Documentation/devicetree/bindings/gpu/arm,mali-valhall-csf.yaml | 1 +
 1 file changed, 1 insertion(+)

diff --git a/Documentation/devicetree/bindings/gpu/arm,mali-valhall-csf.yaml b/Documentation/devicetree/bindings/gpu/arm,mali-valhall-csf.yaml
index 8eccd4338..1d25eeefc 100644
--- a/Documentation/devicetree/bindings/gpu/arm,mali-valhall-csf.yaml
+++ b/Documentation/devicetree/bindings/gpu/arm,mali-valhall-csf.yaml
@@ -18,6 +18,7 @@ properties:
     oneOf:
       - items:
           - enum:
+              - google,gs201-mali         # G710
               - mediatek,mt8196-mali
               - nxp,imx95-mali            # G310
               - rockchip,rk3588-mali
